# Build context for ALL service images is `modules/`. Each Dockerfile
# COPYs only its own subtree (services/<svc>/) plus shared sources
# where applicable (docs/help/ for chat). We exclude only what no
# service container needs, never specific service directories.

# Mobile / web apps and libs — no backend service needs these.
apps/
libs/
plugins/
tools/
web/
mobile

# Per-service noise that should never end up in any image.
# Note: services/*/scripts/ stays — share-video has a postinstall hook
# that copies font subsets; auth/chat don't ship scripts/ so excluding
# would be a no-op for them anyway.
services/*/compose/
services/*/README.md
services/*/fly.toml
services/*/.env
services/*/.env.*
services/*/.povtorenie-work
services/*/*.tsv

# Serverless leftovers — share-* services migrating to containers.
# Their serverless-*.yml / event_adapter.* / layers/ get deleted in a
# follow-up commit; until then, don't ship them into images.
services/*/serverless-*.yml
services/*/layers/

# Build artifacts and language caches.
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/*.egg-info
**/node_modules
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.airflow
**/.vscode
**/logs
**/coverage
**/.next
**/target/

# corpus-mcp go:embed's these bundled MCP-App player HTMLs at compile time, so
# they must survive the blanket **/dist/ exclusion above (last match wins).
!services/lectorium-corpus-mcp/internal/mcp/dist/
!services/lectorium-corpus-mcp/internal/mcp/dist/*.html

# Git + IDE.
.git
.gitignore
